      "final_text": "Done. All 8 requirements are `VERIFIED`, reproduced by the passport.\n\n**Fix:** [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) had 6 Newton steps; the deployed OpenZeppelin routine has 7. I added the seventh `(result + a / result) >>> 1` line, so `sqrt` is definitionally `newtonSqrt 7` (`req_newton_budget` is proved by unfolding plus `rfl`).\n\n**Proofs:** the core is `sqrt_toNat : (sqrt a).toNat = Nat.sqrt a.toNat`.\n- Initial estimate `1 <<< (log2 a >>> 1)` is `2^(log2 A / 2)` via `toNat_log2` and `WordBridge` shift lemmas.\n- With `x0 = 2^(L/2)`, `s = Nat.sqrt A`: `x0 \u2264 s < 2\u00b7x0`, `s < 2^128`.\n- First BitVec step matches `newton A x0` (factor-2 bound `A < 4\u00b7x0\u00b2`, sums `< 2^256`); the remaining 6 steps match via `WordBridge.iter_map_of_sim` under the preserved invariant `s \u2264 b \u2227 b < 2^255` (sums via `add_div_le_of_sqrt_le`).\n- 7 Nat steps reach the root or root-plus-one (`newtonIter_eq_or_succ_of_lt_two_mul` with `b = 128, k = 5`), and `min_div_eq_sqrt` closes it.\n- The other 7 theorems follow: sqrt bounds from `Nat.sqrt_le`/`Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`, `sqrtUp` facts from `sqrtUp_toNat` plus `le_mul_self_sqrt_add_ite`/`sqrt_add_ite_sub_one_mul_self_lt`, mint facts from `firstMint_eq_some`/`firstMint_isSome`.\n\n**Verification:** `lake build Solution` proves 8 of 8 with no `sorry`; `check_candidate` returns `status: VERIFIED` (six kernels, 2001 property-test cases pass, only `propext`/`Quot.sound`/`Classical.choice` axioms); passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`946fd778\u2026`) reproduced by `verify_passport`.",
